.TH MODBUS-CACHE-CTL 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
modbus-cache-ctl \- one-shot control client for the modbus-cache daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modbus-cache-ctl
.RI [ options ]
.IB command " [args ...]"
.br
.B modbus-cache-ctl
.RI [ options ]
< commands
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends one control command (or a batch piped on stdin, one per line) to the
.B modbus-cache
JSON-lines control server and prints the replies on stdout, one per line.
Every invocation lands in the audit trail (prefix \fBCTL\fR).
.PP
The command grammar is the daemon's: \fBset\fR/\fBunset\fR/\fBshow\fR/
\fBhelp\fR (the settings registry), \fBinspect\fR, \fBshow status\fR,
\fBshow connections\fR, \fBshow cache\fR [\fBall\fR], \fBshow version\fR,
\fBclear cache\fR, \fBrestart\fR, \fBshutdown\fR, \fBquit\fR. See
.BR modbus-cache (1)
CONTROL.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-control-port " TARGET"
the control target: a unix socket path or a TCP port. Default
\fB/tmp/modbus-cache-\fR\fI<listen-port>\fB.socket\fR; the
\fBMODBUS_CACHE_CTL\fR environment variable is the same knob.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " S"
wire timeout, seconds. Default \fB5\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-control-token " TOKEN"
the token for TCP control (the daemon must have been started with the
same one).
.TP
.BI \-\-control-token-file " FILE"
the token from a file (the first line); mutually exclusive with
\fB--control-token\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-audit-log " FILE|\-"
the client's own audit trail
(\fB~/.local/state/modbus-cache/audit.log\fR by default).
.TP
.BI \-\-audit-max-mb " N ", \-\-audit-files " N"
the file sink's gated rotation (defaults \fB10\fR / \fB3\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-no-audit-log
disable the client's audit trail.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B modbus-cache-ctl show status
.IP \(bu 2
.B modbus-cache-ctl clear cache
.IP \(bu 2
.B printf 'show cache\\nclear cache\\n' | modbus-cache-ctl
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
every command answered \fBok\fR.
.TP
.B 1
connection or control error.
.TP
.B 2
command-line misuse.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modbus-cache (1),
.BR modbus-cache-cli (1)
